    "texts":[
        {
            "texttype":"Online",
            "textpurpose":"Gallery Label",
            "textentryhtml":"American minimalist Dan Flavin was one of the first artists to explore light as an artistic medium and the first to utilize industrially manufactured fluorescent lights. The drawings seen here represent plans for future sculptures, in which carefully placed bulbs emit a soft glow. Flavin’s seemingly simple, economical arrangements profoundly transform the space in which they are displayed. Instead of discrete objects that respect their own boundaries, Flavin’s sculptures bathe the space around them in light.",
            "remarks":"PBLJan2013rotation.pdf"
        }
